# 3-DoF Planar Manipulator — ROS 2 Control & Real-Time GUI

A ROS 2 Humble simulation of a 3-DoF planar revolute manipulator implementing Cartesian target control, inverse kinematics, smooth joint-space trajectory generation, real-time joint telemetry, and a PyQt5/PyQtGraph visualization GUI.

This project was developed as a take-home technical exercise for the **Robotics Software Engineer — ROS2 & GUI Systems** role at **Kineshia Robotics**.

---

## 1. Project Overview

The system provides a modular ROS 2 architecture for controlling and visualizing a simulated 3-DoF planar robotic arm.

The operator specifies an end-effector target in Cartesian coordinates `(x, y)` through the GUI.

The control pipeline is:

```text
Cartesian Target (x, y)
          |
          v
+----------------------+
|  Controller Node     |
|----------------------|
| Target validation    |
| Workspace checking  |
| Inverse Kinematics   |
| Trajectory planning  |
| Trajectory execution |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|  Robot Backend       |
| SimulationBackend    |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
    /joint_states
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|     PyQt5 GUI        |
|----------------------|
| Live arm rendering   |
| Joint plots          |
| EE telemetry         |
| Target commands      |
| Pick & Place         |
+----------------------+
